# .inspector-ignore — vulnerability suppression allowlist for the node-modules layer
# =============================================================================
# Format: one vulnerability ID (CVE / GHSA) per line. Blank lines and lines
# beginning with '#' are ignored. Each entry is a DELIBERATE, documented
# risk-acceptance — not a blanket mute. Ignored findings are excluded from the
# scan report and do not count towards the vulnerability thresholds configured
# in .github/workflows/deploy-dev.yml and .github/workflows/publish-tag.yml.
#
# Per-finding format:
#   # SEVERITY X.X
#   # Residual risk: <why this finding is acceptable in our project context>
#   CVE-XXXX-XXXXX
#
# Scanned artifact: dist/node-modules-layer/ (production dependencies only)
# Runtime: AWS Lambda (Node.js), no OS/container surface, no shell access
# =============================================================================


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# fast-xml-builder 1.1.4 (transitive: @aws-sdk/xml-builder → fast-xml-parser 5.5.8)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# WHY PRESENT: @aws-sdk/xml-builder pins fast-xml-parser to exactly 5.5.8,
#   which in turn requires fast-xml-builder ^1.1.4.
# WHY SUPPRESSED: Amazon Inspector does not report this finding as high or
#   critical. In the Inspector console it appears as MEDIUM (CVSS v3.1, ~6.1)
#   and therefore does not warrant blocking a deployment. Only the CI/CD scan
#   rates it HIGH, because it applies the GHSA CVSS v4.0 score (8.7). The two
#   ratings disagree on the vector: v4.0 assumes UI:N / VI:H, v3.1 assumes
#   UI:R / I:L. We follow the severity assessment shown in the console.
# RESIDUAL RISK: LOW. The vulnerability allows attribute values containing
#   unwanted quotes to bypass attribute sanitisation during XML *building*.
#   Our Lambdas exchange OCPI payloads as JSON and never build XML from
#   user-supplied input; fast-xml-builder is only reachable through the AWS
#   SDK's internal request serialisation, where the input is SDK-generated.
# NOTE: A fix IS available (1.1.7+), and it is permitted by the existing
#   ^1.1.4 range — only the lockfile entry is stale. Upgrading is preferable
#   to suppressing.
# WHEN TO REVISIT: On the next lockfile refresh, or if Inspector raises the
#   console severity to high/critical.

# HIGH 8.7 (CVSS v4.0, CI/CD scan) / MEDIUM ~6.1 (CVSS v3.1, Inspector console)
# Residual risk: No user-supplied XML is built; fast-xml-builder is reached only via AWS SDK-internal serialisation.
CVE-2026-44665
